ssibility  for many more types of devices that can  be both a mobile device and a productive  device so this is an example of the the  Chromebook the sous Chromebook flip  where you can turn it into a tablet and  you can turn it into a laptop when it's  in a laptop mode you have multi window  in you can do all the types of desktop  applications you want with things like  virtualization you can be able to access  Windows applications as well but then  you flip it into a tablet and you have  all of the great Android applications  that are out there then make it a great  mobile device and so it's no compromises  lastly how do we go beyond mobility and  what do we do there so the first thing  we're doing here is how do we light up  every screen in your business and so  give you another example of this so this  is an example from from a convenience  store you'll notice the board up there  is a is is an ad and it's a promotion  that they have in the store we've now  made it such that it's easier to make  that a digital sign and it's actually  cheaper to make that a digital sign then  to make it a paper sign we release this  thing last year called the chrome bit  which is an $85 little dongle that you  stick into a screen and it turns it into  a sign or a full computer and so we're  now having it such that people are now  thinking can I take any paper sign I  have and turn it into a digital sign  rotate through the right promotions at  the right time depending on what  inventory I want to push at that  particular time and so one example of  this that that we're working with is  coca-cola so coca-cola just announced a  set of pilots with the albertsons stores  what they're going to be doing is in  about 750 albertsons stores in the drink  aisle they'll be putting a 10 inch  chrome screen there will be a chrome  digital sign they can control that  centrally and push out whatever  promotion they want to those signs the  other interesting part is that on top of  that sign there will be an Eddystone  beacon and when an Eddystone beacon does  is it broadcasts a URL from that  particular sign so when the consumer  goes into that drink island says you  know there's a two-for-one special on  coke zero they can pick out their phone  they'll have a URL that will be there  waiting for the  they can click on that URL and get that  coupon and use it at the checkout stand  immediately and coke can actually rotate  that on a daily or even a  minute-by-minute basis depending on what  they want to want to do and so it opens  up a whole set of new possibilities the  next part of this is what about the  kinds of devices that aren't just mobile  devices and go beyond that to things  like wearables so a few examples here  there are things like watches that that  can be there there are things like for  example other types of specialized  devices for particular areas like  barcode scanners various things like  that there is a whole exciting area  around things like augmented reality and  virtual reality so think about augmented  reality where if you give that to a  field service worker the phone can  actually guide them through a very  complicated repair by actually seeing  what's there and being able to point out  to them exactly what they need to do  those are things that are now going to  be possible with with Android but the  exciting thing is all of these devices  that we can't even dream up today and  we're preparing for that world as well  too we have a project called brillo  which is a which is looking to bring  Android and take Android into these  types of new devices and give you a  platform that can extend to that and we  have a project called weed that that  gives you a communication protocol with  between these devices and makes makes it  says that there's a standard way for  data to flow from those devices into the  cloud and let you let you be able to  actually make the Internet of Things a  reality so the the world of devices this  is kind of where I see things going you  know this could be the dominant set of  devices in five years out there so last  thing I want to talk about is the future  this is my daughter Siona she just  started first grade as you can see from  her little side she she came to that she  came to me a few weeks ago and you know  as many of you guys can relate to I  tried to tell her what I do for a living  and she kind of gets that I build  computers and phones but she mostly  thinks I just go to meetings all day but  a few weeks ago she came to me and and  said daddy can I use a Chromebook I said  where did you learn about this she said  yeah I want to log in with my google  apps account  so oh my god this is crazy and so turns  out at her school they have Chromebooks  they use google apps for a lot of the  things they do she's able to log in and  actually personalized her math lessons  or her reading lessons on Acra on a  Chromebook she uses a thing called I  ready to be able to do math at her own  pace she has this thing called Raz kits  which you can use at home to be able to  actually read books and read from a  massive library books anytime she wants  things like that that I never had when  when I was a kid and I think about the  kinds of things she does she expects  that anywhere she is she can be able to  actually listen to any song that she  wants or that she can say ok Google and  be able to actually get any fact that  she wants at any point in time the  amazing thing is you know 15 years from  now she'll probably be an employee of  one of our companies here 15 years from  now she'll be a probably a customer for  many of your companies as well to where  we as changemakers are building the  world for people like her and all of our  kids where the cloud is just intrinsic  it's always there and so the challenge  for us is how do we make that world take  shape and I think with the technologies  that we have in the mindset that all of  you have we can make that happen thank  you I appreciate it
 

